      "line": 267,
      "verdict": "legit",
      "file_sha": "0aa015d1bcbf",
      "reviewer": "agent",
      "reviewed_at": "2026-06-28T07:00:00Z",
      "disposition": "no-fix",
      "evidence": "Real finite computation, not decide-masking of a non-fact. The theorem enumerates all ~1365 pure 3-braid words of length <6, computing each Kauffman/TL3 bracket (Laurent-polynomial arithmetic) to confirm none is simultaneously Brunnian and nontrivial while the Borromean (length 6) is — minimal crossing number = 6. Kernel decide is infeasible: re-verified 2026-06-28 that decide times out at 590s even with maxHeartbeats 4000000 (the docstring already notes nontriviality alone took ~45s by decide). native_decide compiles the decision procedure; its Lean.ofReduceBool/trustCompiler axioms are documented in the docstring and independently cross-checked against the Python enumeration oracle (both yield 6). Cannot be cleared by decide/norm_num/omega without audit-dodging (§1a); honest disposition is native_decide + documented axioms + oracle cross-check."
    },
